\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Remark}
\title{The adjoint mark}
\date{2026-11-13}

\p{Geometric calculus writes the adjoint of a linear map as #{\bar A}.
Mathematical physics writes #{A^*} or #{A^\dagger}. Here an adjoint, and
an ordinary linear involution, is #{A^\dagger}, and the pairing that
represents it is named where the adjoint is defined. The star remains
the dual module and the dual map. The bar remains conjugation and the
declared involution of the ground ring.}
